    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d131-a1">

                <pb facs="0269" n="157" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg157"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign
                            Affairs to Minister Hill</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The
                                Hague</hi></placeName>,<date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-05-11"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 11, 1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 8098.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: Referring to my note of March 27
                    last, No. 4747, I have the honor to inform your excellency that Her Majesty’s
                    Government is of opinion that the nomination of an international commission
                    would be preferable to the calling of a conference to study the opium question
                    in the Far East.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Van Tets van
                    Gourdriaan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
